{"aliases":[],"ancestry":{"derived_from":["urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-7388-77d7-8ecc-83309d3bf277","urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-7389-7589-869e-ab8bf21eaf9b"],"mutation_dimensions":["faction_count","relationship_complexity","neutral_factions","player_reputation"],"observed_in":["monster default_faction field","species-based vulnerability system"],"source_games":["cataclysm-bn"]},"concept_type":"cross_game_mechanic","decision_refs":[],"definition":"A monster AI system where creatures belong to factions, and faction relationships determine hostile/neutral behavior. This creates emergent infighting where different enemy types attack each other, giving players tactical opportunities.","epistemic":{"confidence":"verified","status":"observed"},"evidence_refs":["urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-738b-782b-9011-579e71dd812a"],"exclusion_criteria":["All monsters are uniformly hostile to player only","Faction is purely cosmetic/lore without gameplay effect","Infighting is scripted rather than emergent"],"id":"urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-738b-7c43-b5be-9212983f63af","implementation_refs":["urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-7388-77d7-8ecc-83309d3bf277","urn:roguelike-games-ib:record:01a02637-7389-7589-869e-ab8bf21eaf9b"],"inclusion_criteria":["Monsters have a faction identifier","Faction relationships determine hostility","Monsters can attack each other based on faction","Players can exploit infighting tactically"],"key":"cataclysm-bn/concept/faction-based-emergent-infighting","language":"en","origin":{"actor_id":"cataclysm-bn-factual","kind":"extractor","run_id":"cataclysm-bn-semantic-run"},"record_type":"concept","schema":"rgkb/concept@2","scope":{"scope_kind":"source","source_id":"cataclysm-bn"},"title":"Faction-Based Emergent Infighting"}
